==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Medalist Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Fiend Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Nymph Cat's primary use is to inflict long-ranged Area Attacks, as she lacks any other [[Special Abilities]]. Compared to [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]], her health and standing range are lower and she has a larger [[Hitbox#Subdivisions|blind spot]], but she inflicts more damage, attacks faster and more frequently, costs slightly less and recharges slightly faster, basically acting as a more aggressive version of Vaulter. As is the case with most [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]], defending her should be a priority. The use of meatshields or tanks who let enemy frontliners live to act as stepping stones is most recommended when using this unit.

==='''True Form'''===
Nymph's previously pathetic survivability is much improved by an increase of health by more than 50% in [[True Form]]. This makes Fiend Cat's usage as an individual unit even better than before, but as with other forms should not be freely sent without any forethought. His original usage as a Long Distance rusher is drastically improved, allowing him the possibility of sneaking into the range of a tough backliner, and dealing damage to them a few times.

Against Aku, Fiend Cat might be used to gain terrain on heavily [[Shield]]ed bosses while their Shields are down and can be quite effective against the [[Aku Cyclone]], although he generally tends to struggle against them due to low health, and some Aku enemies having [[Surge Attack]]s or another type of piercing range. Beware that Fiend Cat does not have Shield Piercing – you will need the backup of [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercing Cats]] in order to fulfill his potential as a sniper.

He does face competition with [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], who has higher standing range, an anti-[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] niche and a potential higher damage output with the [[Savage Blow]] talent unlocked, but Fiend has better advantages with his better Long Distance reach and higher base DPS.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Tough Vs''' greatly increases Fiend Cat's survivability even more. While he normally likes to snipe danger from afar with his Long Distance, this [[Talents|Talent]] can give him more of a fighting chance whenever Aku enemies do push into his blind spot and whenever Akus create Death Surges on top of him.

'''Target [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]''' on the other hand, means that Fiend Cat can not only tank more hits from aggressive Angel pushers, but also push them back with a Long Distance attack that can possibly work against the likes of [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and [[Chickful A]] in particular, making him ten thousand times better an investment than a similar [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] unit, [[Stilts Cat (Rare Cat)|Acrobat Cats]]. Due to their lack of Shields, Angel enemies are more vulnerable to Fiend Cat's knockbacks than Aku enemies, so consider unlocking this Talent if you need more anti-Angel defense. This also synergizes well with Tough Vs, giving him a better chance at living even if he gets hit by hard-hitting Angels like [[Angelic Gory]].

'''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' are decent abilities. However, like with most other units, the [[Catseye]] route should take priority over these Talents. Additionally, the Tough Vs Talent should obviously be unlocked before even considering the HP Buff Talent. If you are especially fond of using him, then deciding to invest into either of these will massively increase his usage by increasing the margin of DPS per stack, which synergises particularly well if you boost him in addition to that investment.

'''Resist Slow''' is a situational ability. It could potentially see some use against [[Condemned Peng]], but Fiend Cat doesn't last long enough for this Talent to be worthwhile and all other Aku/Angel enemies with the Slow ability outrange Fiend and can kill him in one hit. Overall, do not invest in this ability.

As a whole, his Talents are a significant improvement for an already situationally outclassed if not good unit to begin with, and can be considered a worthy use of your NP.

==='''Orb'''===
Fiend Cat, against Aku enemies don't rely much on health or damage, but you can give him an Attack Up vs Aku or Angel. If you unlocked his Tough vs Talent, use Resistant to Aku or Angel orb is the best.

